data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1358,"item_id":"fc_00a48087a7f529db016adb685290988191ac24e86404811278","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"inference\":\"R001\",\"packet_sha256\":\"97aec6649bc201b6d7f24043a43ae832691647375f2ccecb6b20d0de962e565e\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Fresh packet-only mathematical review: I read packet.json in full and the declared Audit A, self-containment, and NL0-format rules. My mathematical input boundary is this packet alone plus those procedural rules and fixed logic/calculation allowance; I did not use source proofs or other task material. I make no claim of runtime isolation or external carrier attestation. The packet does not suffice for its stated conclusion. First unsupported implication in argument order: S002 asserts that the summand functions are measurable, hence AEMeasurable, because J_i∩[0,1] is Borel and the coefficient is constant. No permitted calculation or direct input proves measurability of the indicator/constant-times-indicator function. M002 requires AEMeasurability; listing that assertion in an application check is not a proof. This blocks the integral interchange and the subsequent slicing lower bound. There are also local declaration inconsistencies noted in the closure checks.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The cited proposition IDs in R001 are present among the packet inputs. H001 and H002 have the stated roles; M001–M005 and M008–M014 are available conditional premises. This is not source-fidelity verification.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"First unsupported implication: S002 claims each f(i,·)=ρ_i^s·1_{J_i∩[0,1]} is measurable (and thus AEMeasurable) from Borelness of J_i∩[0,1] and constancy of the coefficient. The packet supplies no applicable result or local proof of that measurability fact. M002 cannot therefore be applied as claimed. This blocks the integral/series interchange used to derive the covering-cost comparison and lower dimension bound.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inputs/3/source_contract\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The M002 application depends on an unproved measurability/AEMeasurability result, which is neither a direct input nor a locally established fact. An application note cannot supply the proof of that result.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inputs/3/source_contract\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The final prose claims dim_H(F)=dim_H(E)+1, matching the packet output after identifying F with E×[0,1] and I=[0,1]. This match does not establish derivation.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The argument divides into D=0 and D>0 cases and purports to combine upper and lower bounds, but the S002 lower-bound branch is blocked by the unsupported M002 applicability step.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"M002's required per-index AEMeasurability is not established by the cited fact that the underlying set is Borel: the needed indicator measurability and multiplication step are not proved or otherwise supplied in this packet.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inputs/3/source_contract\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input statements and output statement are available in full in the packet and can be understood without producer proofs. The output is the dimension identity for the product with I=[0,1].\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs\",\"/output/statement\",\"/logic/primitives\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Material inventory/declaration mismatches: local A_i has type 'projection of V_i to ℝⁿ' but its declaration instead defines ν; local c_s is typed as Hausdorff content but its declaration chooses an interval J_i; N_i uses d_i although the stated diameter is d_{j,i}.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/9\",\"/inference/locals/13\",\"/inference/locals/22\",\"/inference/argument/1/objects\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The actual factual use of measurability/AEMeasurability in S002 has no direct-input or earlier-local-proof basis. The assertion that the fact holds is not a derivation, preventing closure of the M002-dependent argument.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/inference/argument/1/uses\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Mathematical conditional judgment: given the externally checked packet/carrier boundary, this packet alone does not suffice, because the M002 application has the unsupported measurability implication identified above. I read only the frozen packet as mathematical task material and the relevant declared Yui rules. I do not certify execution isolation, carrier identity, hash binding, or transmitted-material readback; these are outside this mathematical judgment.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"/inference/applications/1\",\"/warning\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/1/text\",\"finding\":\"Unsupported implication: Borelness of J_i∩[0,1] and constancy of ρ_i^s imply that the summand function is measurable/AEMeasurable. No direct input or local proof establishes this prerequisite of M002. Consequently the integral interchange and ensuing lower-bound argument are not justified.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/locals/9\",\"finding\":\"A_i is typed as a projection of V_i to ℝⁿ, but its declaration defines ν rather than A_i.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/locals/13\",\"finding\":\"c_s is typed as Hausdorff content, but its declaration chooses J_i; this does not declare or witness c_s as typed.\"},{\"location\":\"/inference/locals/22\",\"finding\":\"N_i is defined using d_i although the diameter variable declared in the packet is d_{j,i}; the notation/binding is inconsistent.\"}]}}"}

